    "B": "Decreased conversion of angiotensin I to angiotensin II",
    "C": "Increased secretion of aldosterone from the adrenal cortex",
    "D": "Increased activation of angiotensin II type 1 receptors on vascular smooth muscle"
  },
  "correct_answer": "B",
  "explanation": "ACE catalyzes the conversion of angiotensin I to angiotensin II. Angiotensin II is a potent vasoconstrictor and stimulates aldosterone secretion. Inhibiting ACE reduces angiotensin II formation, thereby decreasing vasoconstriction and lowering blood pressure."
}

{
