        "correction": "Only the power set contains every subset. Many sigma-algebras are smaller."
      },
      {
        "misconception": "Closure under finite unions is enough for a sigma-algebra.",
        "correction": "A sigma-algebra must be closed under countable unions."
      },
      {
        "misconception": "Every collection containing empty set and X is a sigma-algebra.",
        "correction": "It must also be closed under complements and countable unions."
      },
      {
        "misconception": "The Borel sigma-algebra contains only open sets.",
        "correction": "It contains open sets and all sets generated from them by countable unions, countable intersections, and complements."
