        "Content": "Blood pressure is mainly determined by cardiac output and systemic vascular resistance. Cardiac output depends on heart rate and stroke volume, while systemic vascular resistance depends on vascular smooth muscle tone. Blood volume and neurohormonal systems, especially the sympathetic nervous system and RAAS, also play major roles."
