        "topic": "Cancer stem cells and tumor heterogeneity",
        "details": [
          "Cancer stem-like cells often have enhanced DNA repair, drug efflux, and survival capacity.",
          "Tumors contain diverse subclones with different drug sensitivities.",
          "Therapy can select resistant clones, leading to relapse."
        ]
      },
      {
        "topic": "Management strategies",
        "details": [
          "Combination therapy to target multiple pathways simultaneously.",
          "Sequential therapy based on molecular changes during treatment.",
          "Use of next-generation inhibitors to overcome specific resistance mutations.",
          "Biomarker-guided therapy and companion diagnostics.",
